Timeline

  1. Read the beacon OpenAPI at /spec.json BEFORE writing any code. /webhook
     names exactly two properties (source, event), sets no
     additionalProperties:false, and documents 202 and 429 only. Extra fields
     are therefore permitted by the OpenAPI default but NOT documented as
     retained; the payload rides in source/event where it can and the
     structured detail is [H], stated as such in the doc.
  2. wal.sh probed and rejected as a sink: bare and ?deployment= return a
     byte-identical 24586-byte text/html 200. Cannot distinguish stored from
     discarded.
  3. Prior art: docs.datadoghq.com is NULL-ROUTED from hydra (resolves to ::
     and 0.0.0.0, curl (7) on 443) -- recovered from Datadog's own
     GitHub-published OpenAPI. help.bluetriangle.com serves a Cloudflare JS
     challenge -- recovered through the Zendesk Help Center API. The Elastic
     route named in the brief, POST /api/observability/annotations, does not
     exist; the real one is POST /api/apm/services/{serviceName}/annotation,
     confirmed against elastic/kibana source. That one is observed to be
     false, not merely unobserved.
  4. FAILED FIRST: the unreachable-sink run reported "HTTP 000000" and took
     the wrong branch of the case, diagnosing a rejection where there was an
     unreachable host. Cause: code=$(curl ... || echo 000) concatenates
     curl's own "000" with the fallback. Fixed to code=$(curl ...) || code=000.
     Found by RUNNING the path, not by reading the line -- which is the point.
  5. FOUND, NOT FIXED: change/activate.sh line 28 cds into change/ while every
     relative path below it is written from the repo root, so the file cannot
     run from anywhere. Pre-existing, and the arithmetic consequence of
     docs/changing-the-pipeline.org measuring zero invocations of that file.
     The marker call is addressed through an absolute $HERE captured before
     the cd so it does not inherit the defect.

